# =============================================================================
# Lumerical project, log and movie files
# =============================================================================
# Simulation projects are large, binary and machine-specific — the MMI one is
# over 100 MB, above GitHub's per-file limit. They regenerate every time a
# simulation is saved, so there is nothing to gain by tracking them.
# =============================================================================
*.lms
*.ldev
*.log
*.m1v
*.mp4

# =============================================================================
# Python environments and bytecode
# =============================================================================
# The local virtual environment and its caches. `Lib/` is listed separately
# because an in-place `pip install` can leave a stray site-packages directory
# in the repository root, outside `.venv/`.
# =============================================================================
.venv/
Lib/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# =============================================================================
# Editors
# =============================================================================
# VSCode settings are machine-specific. The Obsidian folder holds the vault's
# editor and plugin state, which is not part of the design notes themselves.
# =============================================================================
.vscode/
MZI/.obsidian/

# =============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored
# =============================================================================
# Simulated data (*.mat), result figures (*.png) and the INTERCONNECT data card
# (*.ldf) are tracked on purpose, so that every result in the READMEs can be
# inspected without a Lumerical licence. Do not add them here.
# =============================================================================
